# Capsule-bench ANSWER KEYS — never tracked (this repo is public: github.com/ucb-bar/merlin).
# These are the graded answers; committing them defeats the benchmark. They are REGENERABLE from the
# tracked generators (generate_corpus.py + <target>/generate_*_corpus.py) with the oracle model, so
# untracking loses nothing. The public CONTRACT stays tracked: capsule.interface.mlir + capsule.yaml
# (the op/shape/dtype the agent compiles against) and MANIFEST.yaml.
golden.yaml
expected_instruction_coverage.yaml

# The held-out HIDDEN capsule set is never public — even the interfaces reveal held-out shapes, so the
# entire hidden/ subtree (any target, at any depth) stays untracked and local-only.
hidden/

# The held-out capsule SPECIFICATION (op + dtype + exact shape) is itself an answer: the tracked
# profile sits inside the `merlin/contract/` grant every arm gets read-only, so a holdout specified
# there is readable by the agent under test. The spec lives in an untracked sidecar next to the
# public profile; generate_corpus.py loads it when present and emits no hidden capsules when it is
# absent (which is what a public clone should do).
profiles/*.hidden.yaml

# Whole-model capsule weights (externalized safetensors) — large regenerable binaries produced by
# model2MLIR at generation time; never tracked (the linalg interface + capsule.yaml stay the contract).
capsule.weights.safetensors
*.safetensors
*.safetensors.manifest.json
